==German==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|de|gmh|ratte}}, from {{inh|de|goh|ratta}}, {{m|goh|rato}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*rattaz||rat}}; see that entry and {{m+|en|rat}} for more. Compare also {{cog|nl|rat}}, {{cog|sv|råtta}}, {{cog|fr|rat}}.

The consonantism ''ratta'' in Old High German (instead of *''razza''), along with other hints, makes it likely that the former is borrowed from {{der|de|osx|ratta}}. The dialectal German variant {{m|de|Ratz}} could be reflective of a different Proto-Germanic form, a later expressive derivative, or an Old High German adaptation of the Old Saxon form. 

